{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Test leads and heat shrink tubing fit the work suggested by my breadboards, relay, battery holder, and PCB supplies: making temporary connections and insulating finished wire joints.",
    "The compact caliper feels useful for measuring components and mounting clearances across my small DIY projects. Electronic cleaner and an oscilloscope also fit my electronics interests, though I would wait for a specific need before choosing them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Printer filament and a deburring tool assume fabrication needs that my electronics purchases do not establish; I have no current printing or edge-finishing project.",
    "Springs and locking nuts need a particular mechanism or matching hardware sizes to be useful to me. The larger caliper also adds measuring range I do not currently need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in hands-on electronics seems to have been stretched into a broader interest in fabrication and workshop supplies.",
    "My caster purchase seems to have been treated as a reason to suggest other mechanical hardware, even though it does not tell you which parts I need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My electronics purchases point toward practical connection, assembly, and insulation supplies that support small circuits.",
    "Being interested in an item is different from needing it now: I can use test leads and heat shrink directly, while cleaner and an oscilloscope would depend on a specific task."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my electronics interests, but stretched them into unrelated workshop needs and missed how much my choices depend on an immediate practical use."
}"}
